{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/776087-herald-the-ascendant","id":776087,"title":"Herald: the ascendant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T10:25:36-08:00","id":776087,"title":"Herald: the ascendant","content":"Have you ever fully &quot;won&quot; a world of Darkness story-line before? Where you finally get your happy/tragic/satisfying end as your mage finally ascends reality, your garou dies valiantly in battle to be reborn as a tribal spirit, your vampire dies or reaches golconda or some other big mystical, spiritual, or heroic end allowing them to leave the world behind. In all that time afterward when you play a new character, a new story, and fight a new villain, have you ever looked back and asked that one niggling question, that one little curiosity that is never satisfied no matter what new book comes out or new game you play.<br /> <br /> Have you ever wondered, what happens next?<br /> <br /> What if, while they had their foot out the door and were on they way out, they took a moment to look back. What if for a single moment they saw the real world of darkness for what it was, no lies, no secrets, no shadows hiding the beast within. what would they see before reality got got tired of waiting and pushed them out the door and slammed it behind them.<br /> <br /> And what if, they didn't like what they saw?<br /> <br /> This is just a little personal project that started off as a &quot;what if&quot; story-line that a circle of friends and I came up with, and I thought it would be a neat idea to share with others.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, you are an ascendant. A &quot;former&quot; pawn in the grand workings of creation and managed to find your way out before someone caved your skull in(or possibly because of it). You took one to many looks back and manage to notice something so absolutely, positively, terribly wrong that you couldn't pass on in good conscience, but now you're stuck. Trapped in a pocket of the spirit world, the land after transcendence, or some the void beyond creation, unable to interact with it, fully able to view the world.<br /> <br /> Yet by some strange act of fate, be it an accidental discovery, the masterstroke of a grand plan, or the mysterious working of a powerful ally, you've manage to find an empty vessel. This herald is entirely human in all senses of the term, but empty soulless, either by being born as such or through some horrifying curse. Whatever it was before, your herald is now a glove through which you can effect the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T11:21:39-08:00","id":776112,"title":"","content":"Basics:<br /> <br /> Heralds are entirely human, they were before they became such and still are now, and any form of supernatural vessels are few and far between. As such they have human strengths and weaknesses and no matter how much the ascendant tries they cannot work any amount of their former power threw their vessel.<br /> <br /> Heralds cannot be and can never become mages, their lack of a souls means the have no avatar and thus no link to raw creation. werewolf/vampire vessels are the result of evil magic and never without someone else already using them(typically the one that took their soul in the first place).<br /> <br /> A herald can learn and use any form of linear magic and ritual that a human may learn so long as they go through the processes necessary to use them.<br /> <br /> This can be both a blessing and a curse for the ascendant controlling them as this makes it easy to blend into the world, but at the same time their lack of powers mean that more often than not others are more willing to believe the heralds wisdom is merely the ramblings of a madman rather than the knowledge that could save the world.<br /> <br /> Rules:<br /> <br /> Every creature in the world of darkness has a form of backlash for their actions that serves to balance out their power, be it humanity for vampire, renown for garou, paradox for mages, or even some less obvious sources.<br /> <br /> For Heralds this central codex is willpower. Their will to change fate is what still ties them to reality and willpower is the only thing driving them forward. As they continue to try and change the world, the more they fail an immediate task, the more people who reject their claims as insane gibberish, the less likely it seems that they'll reach their goal, this willpower erodes until eventualy the ascendant gives up and leaves the world to it's own damnation. Every time a character fails, roles a botch, or is placed in a stressful situation they have to make a willpower role. If they fail then they loose a temporary dot of willpower, if they botch or are out of temporary willpower then subtract a permanent dot of willpower.<br /> <br /> Ascendants, as beings who exist outside of reality, are able to see the world from an outside perspective. As such any herald can make a willpower role to obtain information and divine events with successes determining the quality of information.<br /> <br /> 1 success, you know something bad will happen soon<br /> <br /> 2 success, you know where something bad will happen soon<br /> <br /> 3 success, you have a good idea of what someone you should fine looks like<br /> <br /> 4 success, paul seems likely to win the lottery this year<br /> <br /> 5+ success, and the bosses password is...<br /> <br /> Heralds are unaffected by mind or souls altering magics, their vessels are merely puppets guided by the stings of an ascendants will and thus have no mind or souls TO effect, but as trade-off anyone looking for such things will be very curious as to why the herald comes up invisible on their radar.<br /> <br /> Another problem that heralds can run into on their quests for change are probably worst of all, other heralds. As when too heralds meet, the ascendants driving them more often than not try to grab the other vessel for themselves.When this happen both parties enter make opposed willpower roles, difficulty the opponents willpower, with the winner gaining both vessels.<br /> <br /> When all of an ascendants heralds are dead or inaccessible, they loose their last connection to the world and are forced to move on with their world. Vessels are an Ascendants fetters, their avatars, their disciplines, without vessels an ascendant is just a man watching TV impotently raging at things they can't change. That fact that available vessels are few in number only reinforces how precious they are. When a player has more than one vessel, they can choose to play one, leaving the other as an NPC with the same goals, and may switch between them whenever they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-28-2015, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}